    654  f089							; Water band surface drifts 0-3 lines down/up. off = triangle(p),
    655  f089							; p = EnemyRamP>>4 (free-running clock, 16 frames per pixel = gentle
    656  f089							; wave speed): p0-3 = down (0→3), p4-7 = back up (3→0), p8-15 = rest
    657  f089							; (~2.1 s at 0). 256-frame period wraps 15→0 with off=0 both sides (no
    658  f089							; jump). Stores 36+off; kernel .Row row2 uses it, .WaterRow derives
    659  f089							; 47-count. CollisionX is overscan-only elsewhere — this VBL write is
    660  f089							; the last before the kernel read (stomp-zone safe, no new ZP byte).
