   3818  fe14							; ==============================================================================
   3819  fe14							; Phase 5 — second GRP1 object (no flicker). TIA has one GRP1 sprite, so two
   3820  fe14							; objects in a room used to alternate frames (30 Hz flicker each). When they
   3821  fe14							; live in DIFFERENT cave bands each can be drawn on ALL of its scanlines: the
   3822  fe14							; band's setup swaps the live trio (ObjBase/ObjTop/ActiveObjectX) for slot 1
   3823  fe14							; and repositions P1 there. The per-line object path is untouched — it already
   3824  fe14							; draws from the live trio and takes COLUP1 from ObjColorTab[ObjBase+row].
   3825  fe14							;
   3826  fe14							; Invariant (do not relax): slot 1's band is STRICTLY HIGHER than slot 0's.
   3827  fe14							; Bands are set up 0->1->2, so no later band has to restore slot 0's trio.
   3828  fe14							; Rooms whose two objects share a band keep the old behaviour (slot 0 only,
   3829  fe14							; rotation in SelectActiveObject unchanged).
   3830  fe14							; Cost: the band-compare early-out sits in the setup line's free tail (0
   3831  fe14							; lines); a band that DOES host slot 1 pays 2 lines (SetObjectXPos must start
   3832  fe14							; on a line boundary and the HMOVE needs the next line's HBLANK).
   3833  fe14							;
   3834  fe14							; StageSlot1 (VBLANK, after SelectActiveObject): stages ObjBase1/ObjTop1/ObjX1,
   3835  fe14							; $FF = none. Slot 1 = the miner or the first live enemy whose Y is in a band
   3836  fe14							; above slot 0's. The KEY skip mirrors the slot-0 path (KeyHeld = LevelStartRoom
   3837  fe14							; b7). Tally frames ($FE) are gated out: EnemyRamY holds score-pointer bytes
   3838  fe14							; then (AGENTS: tally frame draws the MINER only).
   3839  fe14							; ==============================================================================
   3840  fe14
   3841  fe14		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$FE90 - *, 0	; ObjColorTab/ObjSprites moved to the
   3842  fe90							; $F744 fill (Phase 6: tall art). The $FE8F
   3843  fe90							; end is kept so FoldIndirect stays at $FE90.
   3844  fe90							; BOTH same-page 4c fetches (verify guards);
   3845  fe90							; end $FE8F -> HOF tramp $FE90 (shifted +$10,
   3846  fe90							; mirrors+HOF_ENTRY/LHT_ENTRY synced)
   3847  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3848  fe90							; ObjColorTab — per-scanline GRP1 object colors, stride 8 = ObjSprites
   3849  fe90							; stride; indexed by the same X = ObjBase + r in .Grp1 at $FE00 (4c, same
   3850  fe90							; page for all 72 B — the passing +7 probe's exact cycle sum). Row colors
   3851  fe90							; per OBJ_* slot: type color x8 (matches EnemyColorTable /
   3852  fe90							; SelectActiveObject frame colors — no visual change for enemies/lamp/bomb);
   3853  fe90							; MINER slot = miner.png purple/pink/grey -> nearest NTSC $54/$4A/$08.
   3854  fe90							; NOTE: dark rooms no longer force grey objects — the frame-level $0A write
   3855  fe90							; is overridden per row (no budget for a dark skip flag; see .Line probe).
   3856  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3857  fe90
   3858  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3859  fe90							; FoldIndirect — cross-bank data fetch (HERO fold, write-triggered;
   3860  fe90							; level_bank_plan §0.1). Pad lands $FEF6-$FEFF (last byte ≤ $FEFF — $FF00
   3861  fe90							; stays the fineAdjust anchor). Bytes must be byte-identical in bank2
   3862  fe90							; (guard: verify_build) — after `sta $1FF8` the CPU fetches the remainder
   3863  fe90							; from the data bank at the same PC.
   3864  fe90							; Contract: bank select is ABSOLUTE $1FF8 (bank2) — X/Y both preserved,
   3865  fe90							; A = junk in, data out (`sta $1FF6` switches back, A preserved).
   3866  fe90							; P3.1 deviation (plan §0): `sta $1FF8,X` required X=0, but every enemy
   3867  fe90							; loop keeps the slot in X and has no free temp to swap (DEY/snake hold
   3868  fe90							; Temp live across the read). All level data is bank2, so X-selection is
   3869  fe90							; dead weight; bank3 data later needs a second entry `sta $1FF9` pad.
   3870  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3871  fe90							; E4 moth entry tramp ($FEF0-$FEF5) — byte-identical with bank2's copy
   3872  fe90							; (guard: verify_build check_moth_tramp). bank0 executes `sta $1FF8`; the next
   3873  fe90							; fetch ($FEF3) comes from bank2 = `jmp MothRoutine`. Neither bank runs its
   3874  fe90							; other half: bank0 is switched away at $FEF2, bank2 is never entered here.
   3875  fe90							; The 6-byte pad is the only free hole before FoldIndirect's pinned $FEF6.
   3876  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3877  fe90		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$FE96 - *, 0	; S5.4 LHT entry tramp (byte-identical w/ bank2,
   3878  fe96							; guard: check_moth_tramp — shifted +$10)
   3879  fe96				   LaserHitTest
   3880  fe96		       8d f8 1f 	      sta	$1FF8	; select bank2
   3881  fe99		       4c 00 ff 	      jmp	$FF00	; bank2 LaserHitTestBody (dead in bank0; guard
   3882  fe9c							;   pins operands == bank2.lst label)
   3883  fe9c
